e elements. For example, if we choose G, that covers both 0 and 1, so we cannot choose E or D separately. Similarly, H covers 2 and 3, so cannot choose A or F separately. C covers 3 and 4, so cannot choose F or B separately.\n\nWe need to find all subsets of rows that cover all elements exactly once.\n\nLet's enumerate by considering whether we use G or not.\n\nCase 1: Use G ([0,1]). Then we cannot use E or D. So 0 and 1 are covered. Remaining elements to cover: 2,3,4. We need to cover them with rows that don't include 0 or 1. Available rows that don't include 0 or 1: A [2], B [4], C [3,4], F [3], H [2,3]. Note that G is used, so we cannot use E or D.\n\nWe need to cover 2,3,4 exactly once"}}],"created":1790957877,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3787,"total_tokens":4555,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-CZjMr37tokI6rT4913zGfqhq00sm7gxH","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3787,"prompt_ms":457.562,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12082439926062846,"prompt_per_second":8276.474007894012,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2340.903,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.052024771838331,"predicted_per_second":327.65133796658813}}